  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nWe are minimizing the evaluation function that returns 2*n*max(convolve(a,a)) / sum(a)^2. Our approach is to accelerate the convergence of the optimization process using a trust-region-based Bayesian optimization framework. The key idea is to model the objective function as a Gaussian Process over log-sum-normalized sequences and optimize the trust-region parameters interactively to escape local minima. This helps us find a global minimum faster by balancing exploration and exploitation effectively.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nEach candidate sequence a is represented as normalized and non-negative (sum=1). The objective is the maximum convex value in the full convolution. We compare candidate objectives by their actual value after normalization and clipping. The optimization uses a zero-degree-of-freedom formulated system and an adaptive step-size control mechanism.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nWe initialize with the parent sequence (if provided) and generate initial candidates. Then we set up a Bayesian optimization loop with performance monitoring. For each evaluation, we adjust the trust-region parameters dynamically to focus on promising areas while ensuring non-negativity and boundedness. The final candidate is the one that showed the best improvement during the search.\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Default sequence generation\n- Trust-region expansion/contraction via Bayesian optimization, where the acquisition function and probabilistic confidence are dynamically calculated.\n- This is distinct from the provided approach by using a Gaussian Process-based optimization.\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Time budget: 1500 seconds\n- Initial evaluations not counted toward the budget\n- Repetition of candidate evaluations exits loop without time penalty\n- Robustness is handled by sorting and updating only if the candidate passes direct validation.\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- The entire search is built from scratch with clear stages.\n- Final validation is performed manually and exhaustively.",
